Depends: python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, wl-clipboard, qdbus-qt6, systemd, udev
Recommends: plasma-workspace, kwin-wayland
Conflicts: easy-switcher
Replaces: easy-switcher
Description: fix text typed in the wrong keyboard layout (en/ru) on KDE Plasma Wayland
 Caps Lock fixes the last typed word (erase, switch layout, retype the same
 keys); pressing it again undoes. Shift+Caps Lock fixes the selected text word
 by word, or the whole current line in terminals.
 .
 A sandboxed system service reads the keyboards directly and injects keys
 through its own virtual keyboard. It keeps only the last word and line in
 memory, never writes them anywhere, and ignores password windows and the
 lock screen. Caps Lock is remapped to Pause via udev hwdb.
